{"created": "2026-10-23T09:53:15.019184+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-23T09:53:17.953847+00:00", "id": 23590925, "conceptrecid": "23590924", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23590925", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23590924", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23590925", "metadata": {"title": "Continuous edition v4 \u00b7 card set v7 (B1\u2013B207)", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23590925", "publication_date": "2026-10-23", "description": "<p>The Operator-First Atlas is a map of one way of doing mathematics and physics: start from the operator, follow what its subspaces, spectrum and boundaries keep, and read the physics off what survives. It is organised as eight strata (Calibration, Subspace, Spectrum, Wall, Census, Memory, Volume and Realizations) joined by 207 bridges.</p>\n<p>Each bridge is a single statement that crosses from one stratum to another, or stays inside one. Every bridge carries:<br>- its route and its grade (149 theorem, 34 measured, 6 derived, 10 conjecture, 8 reading);<br>- one drawn figure;<br>- the way across: what to carry, what to check, and where you arrive;<br>- the condition that closes it;<br>- the reason it holds;<br>- a worked witness;<br>- links to the bridges it shares a form with, pairs with or contrasts with.</p>\n<p>Each card stands on its own and can be read, cited or shared separately; together they make one map.</p>\n<p>The atlas is built as a method library. It records new methods and new combinations of existing ones, so that a live problem can be approached from many directions at once.</p>\n<p>This edition runs from the metric&ndash;curvature bound and the geometric wall through:<br>- spectral flow, knot invariants and moduli-space memory;<br>- census and boundary channel counts;<br>- the offset as a log-odds and a rapidity;<br>- horizons, the ISCO and Hawking pairs read as boundary data;<br>- combinatorial results: the biplanar join bound for C\u2087[K\u2084] and the permutation coboundary constant k/3;<br>- the two-books bridges (B183&ndash;B207): non-normality and its opposite as the two halves of one product, odd-loop frustration, the zeta pencil, and the doubled Schwarzschild slice.</p>\n<p>Files:<br>- operator_first_atlas_continuous_v4.html: the complete atlas as one self-contained document, 414 figures, opens in any browser.<br>- atlas_cards_v7_html.zip: one standalone HTML card per bridge.<br>- atlas_cards_v7_png_part1&ndash;4.zip: every card as an image.<br>- atlas_new_cards_B183-B207_v7.zip: the newest cards, B183&ndash;B207.</p>\n<p>Prepared with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic) for drafting, computation and checking; the ideas, the framework and every final decision are the author's.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Beasley, Jeromie", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["operator-first; quantum geometric tensor; projector geometry; non-normal operators; exceptional points; spectral flow; knot invariants; character variety; entanglement Hamiltonian; boundary offset; black hole horizons; graph thickness; coboundary expansion; mathematical atlas"], "resource_type": {"title": "Model", "type": "model"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23590924"}}]}}, "title": "Continuous edition v4 \u00b7 card set v7 (B1\u2013B207)", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23590925", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23590925", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23590925?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23590925", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23590925", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23590925", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23590925/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23590924", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23590924", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23590924", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23590924", "self_